  "notes": "Modified cash basis village with fund columns. Governmental: used Total Governmental Funds column (p5-6); beginning/ending cash = fund balances 1,312,620 / 1,555,561 (p6) (ending net of 163,542 Park Fund deficit cash; total governmental cash assets are 1,719,103 on p4). Reclassification between Park and Nonmajor funds nets to zero. Governmental transfers in 301,222 include 50,000 from the Water Fund (business-type transfers out 50,000). Taxes 275,916 split using General Fund (property 153,302, motor vehicle 27,052) and Debt Service Fund property taxes 95,562 (p10, p20); sums to 275,916. Intergovernmental kept as printed (General 45,515 + Street 158,259 + Debt Service 12,694). Franchises and leases includes public power lease 93,991. Business-type: proprietary funds statement p8 (Water, Sewer totals); receipts = charges for services 196,967 + other income 31,291 (printed no single total; computed); loan proceeds 278,635 in business_type.debt_proceeds; transfers to other funds -50,000; roll-forward 370,313 + 196,967 + 31,291 - 560,003 + 278,635 - 50,000 = 267,203. Sewer fund cash is negative (72,288). Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position totals column (p1); no liabilities shown. Detail: fund budget-and-actual schedules p10-20 (no separate departmental schedules, so no double counting); Nonmajor fund combining statement p9 (Landfill, Hall Deposit) is covered by the fund schedules. ARPA fund p21 has no 2025 activity. Fund types are all governmental in the detail; no business-type detail schedules printed. Read pages 1-21 of 21."
